        `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given to thwart the arising of the other party's claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment`
            `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party asserts claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment`
            `the other party asserts those claims in good faith` IS `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss civilian service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service`
            `the notice was given because the other party fulfils a legal duty` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty`
            `the other party assumed that legal duty voluntarily` IS `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association`
            `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association`
            `the notice was given because the employee lawfully exercises a union activity` IS `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business`
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking`
            `the employer can prove a justified reason for the notice` IS `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal`
            `there is an employee representation` IS `the employees have an employee representation`
            `the employee representation was consulted` IS `the employee representation was consulted`
            `the employees were consulted` IS `the employees were consulted`
        `my facts for Art 336(3)` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` WITH
            `the mandate ended because the employment was transferred` IS `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred`
            `the day the notice was given` IS `the day the notice was given`
            `the last day the mandate would have lasted had the employment not been transferred` IS `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred`
        `my notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` WITH
            `given by` IS Employer
            `facts for Art 336(1)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(d)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(e)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(3)` IS `my facts for Art 336(3)`
        `abusive on a listed ground` MEANS
            `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` `my notice`

-- Art 336a(1). The party that gives an abusive notice owes the other party a compensation: this applies to your employee if your employee gave the notice. Paragraph 2 of Art. 336 speaks only of the employer's notice, so only the grounds of paragraph 1 are read.
@export As the employer, am I owed compensation for the notice my employee gave (Art 336a(1))?
GIVEN `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because of a characteristic that the person who received it holds by virtue of their personality (Persönlichkeit)? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that characteristic connected with the employment relationship?
      `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that characteristic substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right breach a duty arising from the employment relationship?
      `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given in order to prevent claims of the person who received it from the employment from arising? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was thwarting those claims the only purpose of the notice, with no other purpose beside it?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice assert those claims in good faith (nach Treu und Glauben)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service (Schutzdienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service (Zivildienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty (gesetzliche Pflicht)?
      `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice take on that legal duty voluntarily (freiwillig übernommen)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, am I owed compensation for the notice my employee gave (Art 336a(1))` IS
    `Art 336a(1) the party giving notice owes the other party compensation`
        (`Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` `my notice`)
    WHERE
        `the party giving notice` MEANS Employee
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because of a characteristic the other party holds by virtue of personality` IS `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it`
            `the characteristic is connected with the employment` IS `that characteristic is connected with the employment`
            `the characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party exercises a constitutional right` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right`
            `the exercise of the right breaches a duty from the employment` IS `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment`
            `the exercise of the right substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given to thwart the arising of the other party's claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment`
            `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party asserts claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment`
            `the other party asserts those claims in good faith` IS `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss civilian service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service`
            `the notice was given because the other party fulfils a legal duty` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty`
            `the other party assumed that legal duty voluntarily` IS `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given because the employee lawfully exercises a union activity` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
            `the employer can prove a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS FALSE
            `there is an employee representation` IS FALSE
            `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
            `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(3)` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the mandate ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
            `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the last day the mandate would have lasted had the employment not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `my notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` WITH
            `given by` IS Employee
            `facts for Art 336(1)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(d)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(e)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(3)` IS `my facts for Art 336(3)`

-- Art 336a(2). The compensation may not exceed the employee's wages for six months; the judge fixes the amount.
@export As the employer, what is the most I can claim for the notice my employee gave (Art 336a(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because of a characteristic that the person who received it holds by virtue of their personality (Persönlichkeit)? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that characteristic connected with the employment relationship?
      `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that characteristic substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right breach a duty arising from the employment relationship?
      `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given in order to prevent claims of the person who received it from the employment from arising? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was thwarting those claims the only purpose of the notice, with no other purpose beside it?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice assert those claims in good faith (nach Treu und Glauben)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service? (If you gave the notice, that person is your employee; if your employee gave the notice, it is you.)
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service (Schutzdienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service (Zivildienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty (gesetzliche Pflicht)?
      `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice take on that legal duty voluntarily (freiwillig übernommen)?
      `the monthly wage of the employee` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the employee's wages for one month? (Give every amount in the same currency.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the most I can claim for the notice my employee gave (Art 336a(2) and (3))` IS
    `Art 336a(2) and (3) the most the compensation can be`
        `abusive on a listed ground`
        (`Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` `the party giving notice` `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`)
        `the monthly wage of the employee`
    WHERE
        `the party giving notice` MEANS Employee
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because of a characteristic the other party holds by virtue of personality` IS `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it`
            `the characteristic is connected with the employment` IS `that characteristic is connected with the employment`
            `the characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party exercises a constitutional right` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right`
            `the exercise of the right breaches a duty from the employment` IS `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment`
            `the exercise of the right substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given to thwart the arising of the other party's claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment`
            `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party asserts claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment`
            `the other party asserts those claims in good faith` IS `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss civilian service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service`
            `the notice was given because the other party fulfils a legal duty` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty`
            `the other party assumed that legal duty voluntarily` IS `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given because the employee lawfully exercises a union activity` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
            `the employer can prove a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS FALSE
            `there is an employee representation` IS FALSE
            `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
            `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(3)` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the mandate ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
            `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the last day the mandate would have lasted had the employment not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `my notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` WITH
            `given by` IS Employee
            `facts for Art 336(1)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(d)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(e)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(3)` IS `my facts for Art 336(3)`
        `abusive on a listed ground` MEANS
            `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` `my notice`

-- Art 336a(2). The cap applies to the compensation; damages claims on another legal basis are reserved.
@export As the employer, does the cap on compensation apply to the claim made against me (Art 336a(2))?
GIVEN `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What kind of claim is it? Choose one of: compensation under Art 336a; damages on another legal basis; another kind of claim.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, does the cap on compensation apply to the claim made against me (Art 336a(2))` IS
    `Art 336a(2) the cap limits this claim` `the kind of claim`

§§ `Keeping a claim: the objection and the action`

-- Art. 336b. These arise only where the other side claims, or may claim, the compensation: the form can ask "Is the other side claiming compensation for the notice?" first.

-- Art 336b(1). Whoever wants to assert the compensation must object to the notice in writing, with the party that gave it, at the latest by the end of the notice period. Asked of the party that received the notice (your employee, if you gave it).
@export As the employer, is the other side's objection valid (Art 336b(1))?
GIVEN `the other side's objection was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the objection of the party that received the notice (your employee, if you gave it) made in writing?
      `the other side's objection was directed against the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that objection directed against the notice of termination itself?
      `the other side's objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that objection made to the party that gave the notice (you, if you gave it)?
      `the day the other side's objection was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that objection made?
      `the last day of the notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, is the other side's objection valid (Art 336b(1))` IS
    `Art 336b(1) the objection meets the requirements` `my objection`
    WHERE
        `my objection` MEANS `Objection` WITH
            -- Fixed: this question is about the compensation of Art. 336 and 336a, so the claim rests on them.
            `the claim rests on Art 336 and 336a` IS TRUE
            `the objection was made in writing` IS `the other side's objection was made in writing`
            `the objection was directed against the notice` IS `the other side's objection was directed against the notice`
            `the objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS `the other side's objection was made to the party that gave the notice`
            `the day the objection was made` IS `the day the other side's objection was made`
            `the last day of the notice period` IS `the last day of the notice period`

-- Art 336b(1). The objection must be made at the latest by the end of the notice period.
@export As the employer, what is the last day the other side can object to the notice (Art 336b(1))?
GIVEN `the last day of the notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the last day the other side can object to the notice (Art 336b(1))` IS
    `Art 336b(1) the last day to object` `the last day of the notice period`

-- Art 336b(2), first sentence. If the objection was valid and the parties do not agree on continuing the employment, the party that received the notice can assert the claim.
@export As the employer, can the other side assert the claim against me (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `the other side's objection was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the objection of the party that received the notice (your employee, if you gave it) made in writing?
      `the other side's objection was directed against the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that objection directed against the notice of termination itself?
      `the other side's objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that objection made to the party that gave the notice (you, if you gave it)?
      `the day the other side's objection was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that objection made?
      `the last day of the notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
      `the other side and I agreed on continuing the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and the other side agree on continuing the employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, can the other side assert the claim against me (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the party that received the notice can assert the compensation claim`
        (`Art 336b(1) the objection meets the requirements` `my objection`)
        `the other side and I agreed on continuing the employment`
    WHERE
        `my objection` MEANS `Objection` WITH
            -- Fixed: this question is about the compensation of Art. 336 and 336a, so the claim rests on them.
            `the claim rests on Art 336 and 336a` IS TRUE
            `the objection was made in writing` IS `the other side's objection was made in writing`
            `the objection was directed against the notice` IS `the other side's objection was directed against the notice`
            `the objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS `the other side's objection was made to the party that gave the notice`
            `the day the objection was made` IS `the day the other side's objection was made`
            `the last day of the notice period` IS `the last day of the notice period`

-- Art 336b(2), second sentence. An action has to be made pending within 180 days after the end of the employment.
@export As the employer, what is the last day the other side can bring an action (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `the day the employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did, or will, the employment end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the last day the other side can bring an action (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the last day to bring the action` `the day the employment ended`

-- Art 336b(2), second sentence. If no action is made pending within 180 days after the end of the employment, the claim is forfeited.
@export As the employer, has the other side's claim been forfeited (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `the day the employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did, or will, the employment end?
      `the other side has brought an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other side brought an action in court on the claim (an action made pending, anhängig gemacht)?
      `the day the other side brought the action` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the other side bring the action? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know the position of the claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, has the other side's claim been forfeited (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the claim is forfeited` `my action`
    WHERE
        `my action` MEANS `Action on the claim` WITH
            `the day the employment ended` IS `the day the employment ended`
            `an action has been brought` IS `the other side has brought an action`
            `the day the action was brought` IS `the day the other side brought the action`
            `the day asked about` IS `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Keeping my own claim when my employee gave the notice`

-- Art. 336b from the other side. Art. 336(1) covers a notice given by either party, so an employer can be the party that received an abusive notice: it then has the same objection, the same claim and the same two last days as the employee has in the employee's seat (questions 15 to 19 there). This arises only where the employee gave the notice: the form can ask "Did your employee give you notice?" first.

-- Art 336b(1), from the side of the party that RECEIVED the notice (here the employer, whose employee gave the notice; see the comment on question 21 for why the employer can be that party). Whoever wants to assert the compensation must object to the notice in writing, with the party that gave it, at the latest by the end of the notice period. This is the employer's own objection.
@export As the employer, is my objection to my employee's notice valid (Art 336b(1))?
GIVEN `my objection to my employee's notice was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you object to your employee's notice in writing?
      `my objection was directed against my employee's notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your objection directed against the notice of termination itself?
      `my objection was made to my employee, who gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the objection to the party that gave the notice, your employee?
      `the day I made my objection` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the objection?
      `the last day of my employee's notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, is my objection to my employee's notice valid (Art 336b(1))` IS
    `Art 336b(1) the objection meets the requirements` `my objection`
    WHERE
        `my objection` MEANS `Objection` WITH
            -- Fixed: this question is about the compensation of Art. 336 and 336a, so the claim rests on them.
            `the claim rests on Art 336 and 336a` IS TRUE
            `the objection was made in writing` IS `my objection to my employee's notice was made in writing`
            `the objection was directed against the notice` IS `my objection was directed against my employee's notice`
            `the objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS `my objection was made to my employee, who gave the notice`
            `the day the objection was made` IS `the day I made my objection`
            `the last day of the notice period` IS `the last day of my employee's notice period`

-- Art 336b(1), from the side of the party that RECEIVED the notice. The objection must be made at the latest by the end of the notice period.
@export As the employer, what is the last day I can object to my employee's notice (Art 336b(1))?
GIVEN `the last day of my employee's notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the last day I can object to my employee's notice (Art 336b(1))` IS
    `Art 336b(1) the last day to object` `the last day of my employee's notice period`

-- Art 336b(1) and (2), first sentence, from the side of the party that RECEIVED the notice. Art. 336(1) covers a notice given by either party, so an employer can receive an abusive notice from its employee. If the employer objected in writing, to the party that gave the notice, against the notice and at the latest by the end of the notice period, and the parties do not agree on continuing the employment, the party that received the notice (here the employer) can assert the claim. This answers the procedure only, as the employee's seat does for the same question: whether the notice was abusive is asked by the questions on Art 336.
@export As the employer, can I assert my claim for compensation for the notice my employee gave (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `my objection to my employee's notice was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you object to your employee's notice in writing?
      `my objection was directed against my employee's notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your objection directed against the notice of termination itself?
      `my objection was made to my employee, who gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the objection to the party that gave the notice, your employee?
      `the day I made my objection` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the objection?
      `the last day of my employee's notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
      `my employee and I agreed on continuing the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and your employee agree on continuing the employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, can I assert my claim for compensation for the notice my employee gave (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the party that received the notice can assert the compensation claim`
        (`Art 336b(1) the objection meets the requirements` `my objection`)
        `my employee and I agreed on continuing the employment`
    WHERE
        `my objection` MEANS `Objection` WITH
            -- Fixed: this question is about the compensation of Art. 336 and 336a, so the claim rests on them.
            `the claim rests on Art 336 and 336a` IS TRUE
            `the objection was made in writing` IS `my objection to my employee's notice was made in writing`
            `the objection was directed against the notice` IS `my objection was directed against my employee's notice`
            `the objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS `my objection was made to my employee, who gave the notice`
            `the day the objection was made` IS `the day I made my objection`
            `the last day of the notice period` IS `the last day of my employee's notice period`

-- Art 336b(2), second sentence, from the side of the party that RECEIVED the notice. An action has to be made pending within 180 days after the end of the employment.
@export As the employer, what is the last day I can bring my action (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `the day the employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did, or will, the employment end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the last day I can bring my action (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the last day to bring the action` `the day the employment ended`

-- Art 336b(2), second sentence, from the side of the party that RECEIVED the notice. If no action is made pending within 180 days after the end of the employment, the claim is forfeited.
@export As the employer, has my claim been forfeited (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `the day the employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did, or will, the employment end?
      `I have brought an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you brought an action in court on the claim (an action made pending, anhängig gemacht)?
      `the day I brought the action` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you bring the action? (Any date if you have not brought one.)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know the position of the claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, has my claim been forfeited (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the claim is forfeited` `my action`
    WHERE
        `my action` MEANS `Action on the claim` WITH
            `the day the employment ended` IS `the day the employment ended`
            `an action has been brought` IS `I have brought an action`
            `the day the action was brought` IS `the day I brought the action`
            `the day asked about` IS `the day I am asking about`
